rs have highlighted reliability for C, my notes do not contain a direct reliability statement, but we have decision speed and attention.\"\n\nCandidate B: very conscientious (reliability), handles stress well (stress resilience), good at assessing weather (technical), excellent computer skills (technical), but pretentious and wrong tone (communication issues).\n\nCandidate A: anticipates dangerous situations (technical, safety), sees complex connections (cognitive), excellent spatial vision (technical), very good leadership (crew cooperation), but unfriendly (crew cooperation), eats unhealthily (maybe health, not criteria). No explicit stress resilience.\n\nCandidate D: responds to unexpected events adequately (adaptability), can concentrate very well (attention), solves problems extremely well (technical competence), takes responsibility seriously (responsibility), but moody and loner (crew cooperation).\n\nWe need to decide which candidate best fits overall. Considering safety-critical, reliability and stress resilience are crucial. B has conscientiousness and stress handling. D has responsibility and problem solving but moody and loner may affect crew cooperation. A has technical but unfriendly. C has decision quality and attention, but communication difficulty and egocentric.\n\nWe might argue that B's conscientiousness and stress handling outweigh communication tone issues, and B also has technical weather assessment. So B could be strong. Or D's responsibility and problem solving are strong, but moody and loner may be problematic for long flights.\n\nWe need to bring a point that moves discussion. Perhaps we can ask for more info about Candidate B's communication tone impact on crew cooperation. But we can also argue that B's pretentiousness and wrong tone may be serious for crew cooperation, especially on long flights.\n\nWe could also bring up Candidate D's moody and loner traits as concerns for crew cooperation.\n\nWe need to reference existing discussion: others have favored C. We can challenge that by pointing out lack of reliability evidence for C, and highlight B's strong reliability and stress resilience.\n\nThus we can propose shifting vote to B, or at least suggest reconsideration.\n\nWe must include explicit facts: B very conscientious, handles stress well, good at assessing weather, excellent computer skills; but pretentious, wrong tone. D takes responsibility, solves problems, concentrates, but moody, loner.\n\nWe can say: \"Given the safety-critical nature, reliability and stress resilience are top, and B clearly demonstrates both, while C's reliability is not documented in my notes.\"\n\nThus we can change vote to B.\n\nWe need to produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE and METADATA_JSON with vote.\n\nLet's do that."}
